{#
settings/_encryption.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Settings → Encryption: the keyring of issue #28, as far as a person ever needs
to see it.

Everything here is drawn and driven by settings--encryption, because nothing
on it can be decided by the server: whether the keyring is open, which recovery
copy belongs to this browser, what a key's addresses are — all of that is
known only once the browser has opened it. The markup is the frame, in Twig so
its words come from the catalogues; the script fills the parts that depend on
the keyring and shows the forms that apply.

An account that signs in only through single sign-on has no password for
the keyring to hang off (phase 6e): the status card offers it "Set up
encryption" with a passphrase of its own instead, and once that is done a
card to change the passphrase follows the status. Neither is shown to anybody
whose keyring hangs off the password. A session whose keyring is shut is
asked through the shared unlock dialog (crypto/_unlock_dialog.html.twig),
here as everywhere else; the status card keeps a button to ask again.

Four cards, most comfortable first: whether it works, the recovery phrase,
the devices that can reopen it on their own, and — folded away — the keys
themselves for whoever wants to import, export or replace one. Then the
person's S/MIME certificates (phase 6c), which live on the same keyring: a
PKCS#12 file is opened in the browser and its key wrapped there, so this card
is the script's as well. A fifth lists
contacts' keys, which is a different thing — other people's public keys, no
keyring involved — and is the server's own frame (settings/_contact_keys).
After the sending switches comes the Web Key Directory (settings/_wkd), also
the server's: which of the person's keys plMail publishes for others to find.

Accepts nothing: what it needs is the signed-in user and the routes.
#}
{% set button = 'inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 h-9 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium bg-raised hover:bg-hover text-ink border border-line transition-colors cursor-pointer disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed' %}
{% set primaryButton = 'inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 h-9 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong text-accent-ink transition-colors cursor-pointer disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed' %}
{% set field = 'w-full px-3 py-2 text-sm rounded-lg border border-field bg-field text-ink placeholder:text-ink-faint focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent focus:border-transparent transition-colors' %}

<div data-controller="settings--encryption"
     data-settings--encryption-state-url-value="{{ path('app_keyring_state') }}"
     data-settings--encryption-unlock-url-value="{{ path('app_keyring_unlock_current') }}"
     data-settings--encryption-prelogin-url-value="{{ path('app_login_prelogin') }}"
     data-settings--encryption-csrf-value="{{ csrf_token('keyring') }}"
     data-settings--encryption-user-id-value="{{ app.user.id }}"
     data-settings--encryption-email-value="{{ app.user.email }}"
     data-settings--encryption-locale-value="{{ app.request.locale }}"
     data-settings--encryption-min-length-value="{{ constant('App\\Entity\\User\\User::PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH') }}"
     data-settings--encryption-messages-value="{{ {
         statusOpen:        'encryption.status.open'|trans,
         statusLocked:      'encryption.status.locked'|trans,
         statusLockedPassphrase: 'encryption.status.locked_passphrase'|trans,
         statusUnset:       'encryption.status.unset'|trans,
         setupDone:         'encryption.setup.done'|trans,
         tooShort:          'encryption.setup.too_short'|trans({ '%min%': constant('App\\Entity\\User\\User::PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH') }),
         mismatch:          'encryption.setup.mismatch'|trans,
         passphraseChanged: 'encryption.passphrase.done'|trans,
         wrongRootPassphrase: 'encryption.unlock_dialog.wrong_passphrase'|trans,
         statusDisabled:    'encryption.status.disabled'|trans,
         statusInsecure:    'encryption.status.insecure'|trans,
         statusBroken:      'encryption.status.broken'|trans,
         statusLoading:     'encryption.status.loading'|trans,
         keyCount:          'encryption.status.key_count'|trans,
         phraseSaved:       'encryption.phrase.saved'|trans,
         phraseMissing:     'encryption.phrase.missing'|trans,
         phraseCreate:      'encryption.phrase.create'|trans,
         phraseRecreate:    'encryption.phrase.recreate'|trans,
         phraseInvalid:     'encryption.phrase.invalid'|trans,
         phraseOpensNothing:'encryption.phrase.opens_nothing'|trans,
         phraseRecovered:   'encryption.phrase.recovered'|trans,
         phraseFileName:    'encryption.phrase.file_name'|trans,
         phraseFileIntro:   'encryption.phrase.file_intro'|trans,
         wrongPassword:     'encryption.unlock.wrong_password'|trans,
         rateLimited:       'encryption.unlock.rate_limited'|trans,
         devicesEmpty:      'encryption.devices.empty'|trans,
         thisDevice:        'encryption.devices.this_device'|trans,
         lastUsed:          'encryption.devices.last_used'|trans,
         remove:            'encryption.devices.remove'|trans,
         noDeviceStorage:   'encryption.devices.unavailable'|trans,
         primary:           'encryption.keys.primary'|trans,
         makePrimary:       'encryption.keys.make_primary'|trans,
         renew:             'encryption.keys.renew'|trans,
         compromised:       'encryption.keys.compromised'|trans,
         confirmCompromised:'encryption.keys.confirm_compromised'|trans,
         confirmRenew:      'encryption.keys.confirm_renew'|trans,
         created:           'encryption.keys.created'|trans,
         expires:           'encryption.keys.expires'|trans,
         statusActive:      'encryption.keys.status.active'|trans,
         statusObsolete:    'encryption.keys.status.obsolete'|trans,
         statusCompromised: 'encryption.keys.status.compromised'|trans,
         originGenerated:   'encryption.keys.origin.generated'|trans,
         originImported:    'encryption.keys.origin.imported'|trans,
         lockedKey:         'encryption.keys.locked'|trans,
         importDone:        'encryption.import.done'|trans,
         importNoMatch:     'encryption.import.no_match'|trans,
         wrongPassphrase:   'encryption.import.wrong_passphrase'|trans,
         hardwareKey:       'encryption.import.hardware_key'|trans,
         notAKey:           'encryption.import.not_a_key'|trans,
         exportFileName:    'encryption.export.file_name'|trans,
         smimeEmpty:        'encryption.smime.empty'|trans,
         smimeImported:     'encryption.smime.imported'|trans,
         smimeValidUntil:   'encryption.smime.valid_until'|trans,
         smimeExpired:      'encryption.smime.expired'|trans,
         smimeIssuedBy:     'encryption.smime.issued_by'|trans,
         smimeRetired:      'encryption.smime.retired'|trans,
         smimeExport:       'encryption.smime.export'|trans,
         smimeRemove:       'encryption.smime.remove'|trans,
         smimeConfirmRemove:'encryption.smime.confirm_remove'|trans,
         smimeExportPasswordMissing: 'encryption.smime.export_password_missing'|trans,
         smimeWrongPassword:'encryption.smime.wrong_password'|trans,
         smimeNotPkcs12:    'encryption.smime.not_pkcs12'|trans,
         smimeLegacy:       'encryption.smime.legacy'|trans,
         smimeNotRsa:       'encryption.smime.not_rsa'|trans,
         smimeNoKey:        'encryption.smime.no_key'|trans,
         smimeNoMatch:      'encryption.smime.no_match'|trans,
         failed:            'encryption.failed'|trans,
     }|json_encode }}">

    {# ── Status ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.status.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.status.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
        class:      'mb-6',
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            <p class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-ink" data-settings--encryption-target="status" role="status">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-spinner fa-spin text-ink-faint mt-0.5" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ 'encryption.status.loading'|trans }}
            </p>

            {# The dialog asks by itself when this page opens; this is for asking
               again after it was cancelled. #}
            <div hidden class="mt-4" data-settings--encryption-target="unlockForm">
                <button type="button" class="{{ primaryButton }}" data-action="click->settings--encryption#unlock">{{ 'encryption.unlock.submit'|trans }}</button>
            </div>

            {# An account without a password, before it has a keyring: the
               passphrase everything else will hang off. Checked here for
               length and agreement, because the server never sees it. #}
            <form hidden class="mt-4 max-w-md" data-settings--encryption-target="setupForm"
                  data-action="submit->settings--encryption#setUp" novalidate>
                <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{{ 'encryption.setup.heading'|trans }}</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mb-2">{{ 'encryption.setup.intro'|trans }}</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-danger mb-3" role="note">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ 'encryption.setup.warning'|trans }}
                </p>
                <label for="encryption-setup-passphrase" class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mb-1">{{ 'encryption.setup.passphrase'|trans }}</label>
                <input type="password" id="encryption-setup-passphrase" required autocomplete="new-password"
                       data-settings--encryption-target="setupPassphrase" data-action="input->settings--encryption#clearValidity" class="{{ field }}">
                <label for="encryption-setup-repeat" class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-2 mb-1">{{ 'encryption.setup.repeat'|trans }}</label>
                <input type="password" id="encryption-setup-repeat" required autocomplete="new-password"
                       data-settings--encryption-target="setupRepeat" data-action="input->settings--encryption#clearValidity" class="{{ field }}">
                <button type="submit" class="{{ primaryButton }} mt-3">{{ 'encryption.setup.submit'|trans }}</button>
                <p hidden class="mt-2 text-xs text-danger" data-settings--encryption-target="setupError" role="alert"></p>
            </form>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── Encryption passphrase ───────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# Only for a keyring that hangs off a passphrase, and only while it is
       open: the current passphrase opens the keys, the new one wraps them, all
       in the browser. Changing the sign-in password never comes near this. #}
    <div hidden data-settings--encryption-target="passphraseCard">
        {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
            heading:    'encryption.passphrase.heading'|trans,
            subheading: 'encryption.passphrase.subheading'|trans,
            padded:     true,
            class:      'mb-6',
        } %}
            {% block body %}
                <form class="max-w-md" data-action="submit->settings--encryption#changePassphrase" novalidate>
                    <label for="encryption-passphrase-current" class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mb-1">{{ 'encryption.passphrase.current'|trans }}</label>
                    <input type="password" id="encryption-passphrase-current" required autocomplete="off"
                           data-settings--encryption-target="passphraseCurrent" class="{{ field }}">
                    <label for="encryption-passphrase-new" class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-2 mb-1">{{ 'encryption.passphrase.new'|trans }}</label>
                    <input type="password" id="encryption-passphrase-new" required autocomplete="new-password"
                           data-settings--encryption-target="passphraseNew" data-action="input->settings--encryption#clearValidity" class="{{ field }}">
                    <label for="encryption-passphrase-repeat" class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-2 mb-1">{{ 'encryption.passphrase.repeat'|trans }}</label>
                    <input type="password" id="encryption-passphrase-repeat" required autocomplete="new-password"
                           data-settings--encryption-target="passphraseRepeat" data-action="input->settings--encryption#clearValidity" class="{{ field }}">
                    <button type="submit" class="{{ button }} mt-3">{{ 'encryption.passphrase.submit'|trans }}</button>
                    <p hidden class="mt-2 text-xs" data-settings--encryption-target="passphraseResult" role="status"></p>
                </form>
            {% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}
    </div>

    {# ── Recovery phrase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.phrase.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.phrase.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
        class:      'mb-6',
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            <div data-settings--encryption-target="openOnly" hidden>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink mb-3" data-settings--encryption-target="phraseState"></p>

                <button type="button" class="{{ button }}" data-settings--encryption-target="phraseCreate"
                        data-action="click->settings--encryption#createPhrase"></button>

                <div hidden class="mt-4" data-settings--encryption-target="phraseBox">
                    <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted mb-2">{{ 'encryption.phrase.shown_once'|trans }}</p>
                    <code data-settings--encryption-target="phraseWords"
                          class="block rounded-lg bg-zinc-500/10 px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-mono text-ink select-all leading-relaxed"></code>
                    <button type="button" class="{{ primaryButton }} mt-3" data-action="click->settings--encryption#downloadPhrase">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-download text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {{ 'encryption.phrase.download'|trans }}
                    </button>
                </div>

                <form hidden class="mt-6 max-w-md border-t border-line pt-4" data-settings--encryption-target="recoverForm"
                      data-action="submit->settings--encryption#recover">
                    <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{{ 'encryption.phrase.recover_heading'|trans }}</h3>
                    <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted mb-2">{{ 'encryption.phrase.recover_hint'|trans }}</p>
                    <textarea rows="3" required autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
                              data-settings--encryption-target="recoverWords" class="{{ field }} font-mono"></textarea>
                    <button type="submit" class="{{ primaryButton }} mt-2">{{ 'encryption.phrase.recover_submit'|trans }}</button>
                    <p hidden class="mt-2 text-xs" data-settings--encryption-target="recoverResult" role="status"></p>
                </form>
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── Known devices ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.devices.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.devices.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
        class:      'mb-6',
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            <div data-settings--encryption-target="openOnly" hidden>
                <ul class="divide-y divide-line" data-settings--encryption-target="devices"></ul>
                <button type="button" hidden class="{{ button }} mt-3" data-settings--encryption-target="rememberDevice"
                        data-action="click->settings--encryption#rememberDevice">
                    {{ 'encryption.devices.remember'|trans }}
                </button>
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── Keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.keys.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.keys.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
        class:      'mb-6',
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            <div data-settings--encryption-target="openOnly" hidden>
                <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
                    <form data-action="submit->settings--encryption#importKeys">
                        <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{{ 'encryption.import.heading'|trans }}</h3>
                        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted mb-2">{{ 'encryption.import.hint'|trans }}</p>
                        <input type="file" accept=".asc,.gpg,.key,.txt,application/pgp-keys"
                               data-settings--encryption-target="importFile"
                               class="block w-full text-xs text-ink-muted mb-2">
                        <textarea rows="3" spellcheck="false" placeholder="-----BEGIN PGP PRIVATE KEY BLOCK-----"
                                  data-settings--encryption-target="importText" class="{{ field }} font-mono text-xs"></textarea>
                        <label class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-2 mb-1" for="encryption-import-passphrase">{{ 'encryption.import.passphrase'|trans }}</label>
                        <input type="password" id="encryption-import-passphrase" autocomplete="off"
                               data-settings--encryption-target="importPassphrase" class="{{ field }}">
                        <button type="submit" class="{{ button }} mt-2">{{ 'encryption.import.submit'|trans }}</button>
                        <p hidden class="mt-2 text-xs" data-settings--encryption-target="importResult" role="status"></p>
                    </form>

                    <form data-action="submit->settings--encryption#exportKeys">
                        <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{{ 'encryption.export.heading'|trans }}</h3>
                        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted mb-2">{{ 'encryption.export.hint'|trans }}</p>
                        <label class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mb-1" for="encryption-export-passphrase">{{ 'encryption.export.passphrase'|trans }}</label>
                        <input type="password" id="encryption-export-passphrase" required minlength="8" autocomplete="new-password"
                               data-settings--encryption-target="exportPassphrase" class="{{ field }}">
                        <button type="submit" class="{{ button }} mt-2">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-download text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            {{ 'encryption.export.submit'|trans }}
                        </button>
                    </form>
                </div>

                <details class="mt-6 border-t border-line pt-4">
                    <summary class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink cursor-pointer">{{ 'encryption.keys.advanced'|trans }}</summary>
                    <ul class="mt-3 divide-y divide-line" data-settings--encryption-target="keys"></ul>
                </details>
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── S/MIME certificates ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# The person's own certificates, from PKCS#12 files. Opened in the browser
       (crypto/smime.js), the key wrapped under the user key there; the list
       is the keyring's, so it is drawn by the script like the keys above. #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.smime.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.smime.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
        class:      'mb-6',
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            <div data-settings--encryption-target="openOnly" hidden>
                <ul class="divide-y divide-line mb-4" data-settings--encryption-target="smimeList" data-testid="smime-certificates"></ul>

                <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
                    <form data-action="submit->settings--encryption#importSmime">
                        <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{{ 'encryption.smime.import_heading'|trans }}</h3>
                        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted mb-2">{{ 'encryption.smime.import_hint'|trans }}</p>
                        <input type="file" required accept=".p12,.pfx,application/x-pkcs12"
                               aria-label="{{ 'encryption.smime.file'|trans }}"
                               data-settings--encryption-target="smimeFile"
                               data-testid="smime-file"
                               class="block w-full text-xs text-ink-muted mb-2">
                        <label class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mb-1" for="encryption-smime-password">{{ 'encryption.smime.password'|trans }}</label>
                        <input type="password" id="encryption-smime-password" autocomplete="off"
                               data-settings--encryption-target="smimePassword" class="{{ field }}">
                        <button type="submit" class="{{ button }} mt-2">{{ 'encryption.smime.import_submit'|trans }}</button>
                        <p hidden class="mt-2 text-xs" data-settings--encryption-target="smimeResult" role="status" data-testid="smime-result"></p>
                    </form>

                    <div>
                        <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{{ 'encryption.smime.export_heading'|trans }}</h3>
                        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-muted mb-2">{{ 'encryption.smime.export_hint'|trans }}</p>
                        <label class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mb-1" for="encryption-smime-export-password">{{ 'encryption.smime.export_password'|trans }}</label>
                        <input type="password" id="encryption-smime-export-password" minlength="8" autocomplete="new-password"
                               data-settings--encryption-target="smimeExportPassword" class="{{ field }}">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── Contacts' keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# Not behind openOnly: public keys, which the server shows without the
       keyring — see settings/_contact_keys. Its own request, so the four
       cards above do not wait on it; not loading="lazy", because the card is
       a link target from the reading banner, and a lazy frame below the fold
       had nothing in it to scroll to. #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'contact_keys.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'contact_keys.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            <turbo-frame id="contact-keys" src="{{ path('app_contact_keys_index') }}">
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">{{ 'contact_keys.loading'|trans }}</p>
            </turbo-frame>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── Decrypted mail on this server ───────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# Phase 3b of #28: off unless chosen, per account. See DecryptedMail. #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.decrypted.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.decrypted.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            {{ include('settings/_decrypted_mail.html.twig') }}
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── Sending ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.sending.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.sending.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            {{ include('settings/_encryption_sending.html.twig', { user: app.user }) }}
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {# ── Web Key Directory ───────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# Phase 6d of #28: the person's key, published under the installation's
       own domains for mail programs to find. See WkdDirectory. #}
    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'encryption.wkd.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'encryption.wkd.subheading'|trans,
        padded:     true,
        class:      'mt-6',
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            {{ include('settings/_wkd.html.twig') }}
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}
</div>
